s/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_apply_batch_drift_tolerance.py:329 `with pytest.raises(applier.HeadDriftError)` and :247 `applier._apply_batch(...)`","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conflict/test_conflict_filing_deferred.py:188 `monkeypatch.setattr(applier, \"_apply_batch\", ...)`","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_cross_project_guard.py:129 `pytest.raises(applier_mod.CrossProjectTargetError)`","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_snapshot_differ_stale_local_state.py:113 `monkeypatch.setattr(run_differs_mod, \"_run_differs_outbound\", ...)`","monkeypatch/patch against a module attribute only takes effect if the caller looks the name up on that module at call time; a moved-and-not-re-exported symbol silently defeats the patch or raises AttributeError"],"finding":"The plan claims test updates are 'import-path updates only; no assertion changes', but multiple unit tests patch/reference the to-be-moved symbols through the ORIGINAL module namespace (e.g. patch.object/monkeypatch.setattr(applier, '_apply_batch', ...), pytest.raises(applier.HeadDriftError) / applier.CrossProjectTargetError, monkeypatch.setattr(run_differs_mod, '_run_differs_outbound', ...)). Behavior preservation for these requires re-exporting the moved symbol back into the original module AND having the internal caller resolve it via the module namespace — a constraint the plan neither enumerates nor commits to.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb1276fbb070341bf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ — import-path updates only; no assertion changes'; Approach (applier/run_differs bullets)","norm_id":"n9927a763d9ab2c64","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author moves _apply_batch to a sibling and updates only the import; monkeypatch.setattr(applier, '_apply_batch') no longer affects the real call path, so the deferred-bug-filing and drift-tolerance tests silently pass/fail incorrectly","HeadDriftError/CrossProjectTargetError moved without re-export -> pytest.raises(applier.HeadDriftError) raises AttributeError at collection"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add to the Approach/Scope that any symbol relocated out of applier.py/run_differs.py must be re-exported into the original module (e.g. `from ._sibling import _apply_batch`) and that internal call sites keep resolving it through the module namespace, so existing monkeypatch/patch.object and pytest.raises(applier.<Name>) tests continue to hold without assertion changes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Note the in-package consumer batch_dispatch.py:425 (`applier.HeadDriftError` via lazy_load) and require HeadDriftError to remain resolvable as `applier.HeadDriftError` after any relocation.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py:425 `return (applier.HeadDriftError, pass_io.RescheduleError, urllib.error.HTTPError)` with `applier = lazy_load(\"rebar_reconciler.applier\", \"applier.py\")` at :423"],"finding":"The in-dir facade batch_dispatch.py accesses `applier.HeadDriftError` via lazy_load of the applier module. If HeadDriftError is relocated (the 'cross-project/drift cluster' option), this attribute access breaks unless the class is re-exported into applier. The plan's blanket 'only internal call sites move' does not name this specific runtime attribute dependency inside the reconciler package.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3f5fe580c20f3753","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach: applier.py bullet ('HeadDriftError ... into a sibling module')","norm_id":"nfa496102ae0b3a2a","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Drift cluster is chosen for extraction; batch_dispatch's benign-error-tuple resolution raises AttributeError on applier.HeadDriftError during a live pass"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-derive the move inventory for each relocated symbol from `find_referencing_symbols` AND a string-name grep sweep (covering `monkeypatch.setattr`/`patch.object` targets like `run_differs_mod._run_differs_outbound`, `applier._recheck_drift`, `applier._apply_batch`, `applier.HeadDriftError` and cross-module imports in `outbound_mutation_builders.py`/`batch_dispatch.py`), and state whether each relocated symbol stays re-bound in its original module namespace so string-keyed patches and `module.Symbol` accesses keep resolving.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope: 'extract the named clusters into new sibling modules and update imports only' / 'tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ — import-path updates only; no assertion changes'","Plan Approach: 'Public entry points and import paths keep working; only internal call sites move.'","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_snapshot_differ_stale_local_state.py:113 `monkeypatch.setattr(run_differs_mod, \"_run_differs_outbound\", ...)` (also test_run_differs_wires_refresh_scoped_snapshot_79a4.py:89, test_ticket_plan_shadow.py:426) — string-keyed patch on the ORIGINAL module, invisible to LSP structural refs","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_live_mode_failure_tally.py:677 `monkeypatch.setattr(applier, \"_recheck_drift\", hostile_drift)` — string-keyed patch that breaks if `_recheck_drift` leaves applier's namespace","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py:20-28 imports `_effective_create_defaults_for`, `_effective_link_map_for`, `_effective_priority_map_for`, `_effective_status_map_for`, `_effective_type_map_for` from `outbound_differ` — a production consumer not named in the plan","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py:425 `return (applier.HeadDriftError, ...)` — production attribute access on `applier` for a symbol the plan proposes moving out of applier"],"finding":"The plan enumerates the affected inventory for the relocated symbols as `src` 'imports only' and `tests` 'import-path updates only; no assertion changes', but that inventory omits string-based dynamic references (monkeypatch/patch.object by attribute name on the ORIGINAL module) and cross-module production imports that the LSP does not surface and that 'import paths keep working' does not cover.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd14ce0dca845b427","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/ — extract the named clusters into new sibling modules and update imports only' and 'tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ — import-path updates only; no assertion changes'","norm_id":"n22a14f898bf130c8","priority":0.8,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If `_run_differs_outbound` moves to a sibling and is not re-bound into `run_differs`'s namespace, the three `monkeypatch.setattr(run_differs_mod, \"_run_differs_outbound\", ...)` tests patch a stale name while `run_differs` calls the real relocated function — the stub silently no-ops and the test's intended isolation is lost.","If the drift cluster (`HeadDriftError`, `_recheck_drift`) moves out of `applier.py`, `batch_dispatch.py:425`'s `applier.HeadDriftError` and `test_live_mode_failure_tally.py:677`'s `monkeypatch.setattr(applier, \"_recheck_drift\", ...)` break — a production import cycle-guard and a test both reference these via the `applier` namespace, not via the new module.","If the effective-mapping resolvers move out of `outbound_differ.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py` (a file NOT listed as touched) must have its `from rebar_reconciler.outbound_differ import _effective_*` statements rewritten; the plan's 'imports only' scope names only the two extracted modules, so this consumer's import is silently under-delivered."],"severity":"critical","suggest